.TH IFCONFIG 1
.SH NAME
ifconfig \- inspect or configure the Ethernet interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ifconfig
.RI [ eth0 " [ADDRESS] [netmask MASK] [gateway ADDRESS] [up|down]]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without configuration operands, print the address, mask, gateway and link
state of eth0. Addresses use numeric dotted-decimal IPv4. Configuration
requires root and lasts until reboot. Changing configuration invalidates
existing connections. Down disables protocol traffic; up enables it again.
.PP
The default is 192.168.64.250/24 with gateway 192.168.64.1. The macOS launcher
defaults to shared/NAT internet access. Use --net host for a host-only link,
or --net off to boot offline. DNS servers are in /etc/resolv.conf and local
aliases in /etc/hosts. DHCP is not implemented by this port.
.SH SEE ALSO
ping(1), telnet(1), telnetd(1)
